{
  "info": {
    "name": "Zero-Trust AI Gateway",
    "_postman_id": "zero-trust-ai-gateway",
    "description": "Collection for the Zero-Trust AI Gateway — covers auth-service token issuance (client credentials + authorization code) and all ai-gateway endpoints.\n\n**Client Credentials flow (service-to-service)**:\n1. Run \"Get Access Token (Client Credentials)\" → token saved to `{{access_token}}`\n2. Use any secured request — Bearer token applied automatically\n\n**Authorization Code flow (human user login)**:\n1. Open \"Get Access Token (Authorization Code)\" → click \"Get New Access Token\" in the Auth tab\n2. Postman opens a browser window → log in as alice/bob/etc.\n3. Token (with tier claim) is saved to `{{access_token}}`\n\n**Local profile** (auth disabled): skip step 1 and send requests directly.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "gateway_base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "auth_base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:9000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "client_id",
      "value": "ai-gateway-client",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "client_secret",
      "value": "secret",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "redirect_uri",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081/login/oauth2/code/ai-gateway-client",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "refresh_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "auth_code",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth Service — Client Credentials",
      "description": "Machine-to-machine token issuance. No user login required.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Access Token (Client Credentials)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "    pm.test('access_token is present', () => pm.expect(json.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "    pm.test('token_type is Bearer', () => pm.expect(json.token_type).to.eql('Bearer'));",
                  "    pm.test('expires_in is ~3600', () => pm.expect(json.expires_in).to.be.closeTo(3600, 10));",
                  "    console.log('Token saved to collection variable access_token');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{client_secret}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "gateway.read", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Issues a JWT using client credentials (no user). Token has no `tier` claim — the gateway treats machine tokens as free tier. Token is saved to `{{access_token}}`."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — token issued",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "body": {
                  "mode": "urlencoded",
                  "urlencoded": [
                    { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials" },
                    { "key": "scope", "value": "gateway.read" }
                  ]
                },
                "url": { "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/token" }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "body": "{\n  \"access_token\": \"eyJ...\",\n  \"token_type\": \"Bearer\",\n  \"expires_in\": 3600,\n  \"scope\": \"gateway.read\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Bad Credentials (expect 401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Returns 401 for bad credentials', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "wrong-secret", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies that an invalid client secret is rejected with 401."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth Service — Authorization Code Flow",
      "description": "Human user login via LDAP. The resulting JWT contains a `tier` claim (`free` or `premium`) based on the user's LDAP group.\n\n**Seed users:**\n| User | Password | Tier |\n|------|----------|------|\n| alice | alice123 | free |\n| charlie | charlie123 | free |\n| diana | diana123 | free |\n| eve | eve123 | free |\n| frank | frank123 | free |\n| bob | bob123 | premium |\n| grace | grace123 | premium |\n| henry | henry123 | premium |\n| isabella | isabella123 | premium |\n| james | james123 | premium |\n\n**How to use in Postman:**\n1. Open \"Get Token via Authorization Code\"\n2. Go to the **Auth** tab — it is pre-configured with the authorization_code grant\n3. Click **Get New Access Token**\n4. Postman opens a browser → log in with any seed user\n5. Token is returned and saved to `{{access_token}}`",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Token via Authorization Code",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// This request uses Postman's built-in OAuth2 helper (Auth tab).",
                  "// After clicking 'Get New Access Token' and logging in, Postman",
                  "// completes the code exchange automatically.",
                  "// Use the Pre-request Script or manually copy the token to {{access_token}}.",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (json.access_token) {",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "        if (json.refresh_token) {",
                  "            pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', json.refresh_token);",
                  "        }",
                  "        pm.test('access_token present', () => pm.expect(json.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "        pm.test('refresh_token present', () => pm.expect(json.refresh_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "        console.log('Tokens saved. Decode the JWT at jwt.io to verify the tier claim.');",
                  "    }",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "oauth2",
              "oauth2": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "authorization_code", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "authUrl", "value": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/authorize", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "accessTokenUrl", "value": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/token", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "clientId", "value": "{{client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "clientSecret", "value": "{{client_secret}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "redirect_uri", "value": "{{redirect_uri}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "openid profile gateway.read", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "useBrowser", "value": true, "type": "boolean" },
                { "key": "addTokenTo", "value": "header", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "tokenName", "value": "AI Gateway User Token", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "challengeAlgorithm", "value": "S256", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/actuator/health",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Use the **Auth** tab → **Get New Access Token** to trigger the authorization code + PKCE flow. Postman opens a browser, you log in with a seed user (e.g. bob/bob123 for premium), and the token is returned with `\"tier\": \"premium\"` in the JWT payload.\n\nDecode the token at https://jwt.io to inspect the `tier` claim."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Exchange Auth Code for Token (manual)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "    if (json.refresh_token) {",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', json.refresh_token);",
                  "    }",
                  "    pm.test('access_token present', () => pm.expect(json.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "    pm.test('refresh_token present', () => pm.expect(json.refresh_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "    pm.test('id_token present', () => pm.expect(json.id_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "    console.log('Tokens saved. access_token and refresh_token updated.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{client_secret}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "authorization_code", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "code", "value": "{{auth_code}}", "type": "text", "description": "Paste the code from the browser redirect here, or set the auth_code collection variable" },
                { "key": "redirect_uri", "value": "{{redirect_uri}}", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Manual code exchange — use this if you want to handle the browser redirect yourself.\n\n1. Open this URL in a browser:\n   `http://localhost:9000/oauth2/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=ai-gateway-client&redirect_uri=http://localhost:8081/login/oauth2/code/ai-gateway-client&scope=openid%20profile%20gateway.read`\n2. Log in with a seed user\n3. Copy the `code` parameter from the redirect URL\n4. Set `{{auth_code}}` collection variable to that value\n5. Send this request\n\nThe access_token and refresh_token are saved automatically."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — tokens issued",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "body": "{\n  \"access_token\": \"eyJ...\",\n  \"refresh_token\": \"eyJ...\",\n  \"id_token\": \"eyJ...\",\n  \"token_type\": \"Bearer\",\n  \"expires_in\": 3600,\n  \"scope\": \"openid profile gateway.read\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Access Token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "    if (json.refresh_token) {",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', json.refresh_token);",
                  "    }",
                  "    pm.test('new access_token issued', () => pm.expect(json.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "    console.log('access_token refreshed successfully.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{client_secret}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "refresh_token", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "refresh_token", "value": "{{refresh_token}}", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges a refresh token for a new access token. Refresh tokens are valid for 7 days and are rotated on each use (`{{refresh_token}}` is updated automatically). Run \"Exchange Auth Code for Token\" first to populate `{{refresh_token}}`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Authorize URL (open in browser)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={{client_id}}&redirect_uri={{redirect_uri}}&scope=openid%20profile%20gateway.read",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "authorize"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "response_type", "value": "code" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{client_id}}" },
                { "key": "redirect_uri", "value": "{{redirect_uri}}" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "openid profile gateway.read" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Initiates the authorization code flow. Sending this in Postman will redirect to the login form. Copy the resulting `code` from the redirect URL and paste it into `{{auth_code}}`, then run \"Exchange Auth Code for Token\".\n\nTip: open this URL directly in a browser for a smoother experience."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth Service — Discovery",
      "description": "Public endpoints — no authentication required.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "OIDC Discovery",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/.well-known/openid-configuration",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": [".well-known", "openid-configuration"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the OIDC discovery document — lists supported endpoints, algorithms, and scopes."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "JWKS (Public Keys)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/oauth2/jwks",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "jwks"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the RSA public key(s) used to sign JWTs. The ai-gateway fetches this to validate incoming tokens."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Auth Service Health",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{auth_base_url}}/actuator/health",
              "host": ["{{auth_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Health check — returns `{\"status\":\"UP\"}` when the auth service is running."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "AI Gateway — Chat",
      "description": "POST /api/chat — classify prompt and route to the appropriate specialist LLM.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Chat — Programming Query",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('response field present', () => pm.expect(json.response).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('category field present', () => pm.expect(json.category).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"prompt\": \"Write a binary search algorithm in Java.\"\n}",
